RF.put("questb:b47",{"8847":{"id":8847,"t":"Ten Signets for War Supplies","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8527":{"id":8527,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Roast Raptor!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 roast raptor to Sarah Sadwhistle at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Roast Raptor","desc":"Hi again ‹class›. I can tell you're very excited about all of this. So I suppose you want to bring me another twenty roast raptor. Great. Well you do that. I guess I'll see you when you get back.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.4,"n":"Sarah Sadwhistle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8607":{"id":8607,"t":"The Horde Needs Mageweave Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 57.","obj":"Bring 20 Mageweave Bandages to Lady Callow at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Mageweave Bandage","desc":"I trust that you are speaking to me because you are going to help with the collection I have been entrusted to? Good! By whatever means, and I do mean whatever, I wish for you to gather up a good number of mageweave bandages. Fresh would be nice, but not absolutely necessary. Return them to me here, ‹class›, and I will personally see to it that you are properly rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Do not fail and make me look bad, ‹class›! Return here as quickly as possible with the mageweave bandages we discussed.","done":"Surprising, yet acceptable. Perhaps I underestimated your 'abilities', ‹class›. Perhaps. You completed a very simple task, and for doing so you are to be rewarded out of proportion. But don't let it go to your head. If you really want to prove yourself you should get out there and bring me another bundle of mageweave bandages.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.2,"y":75.1,"n":"Lady Callow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6847":{"id":6847,"t":"Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye from the Winterax caves and return it to Master Ryson.\nBe warned, it is said that Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye carries with it a terrible curse!","desc":"Your war in the heart of Alterac means nothing to the Syndicate, ‹class›. We will do as we have always done: Wait until a clear victor rises from the ashes and rubble of this madness and then strike.\nThat, however, is not why we are here now. The All Seeing Eye has been lost - taken by the Winterax trolls of the region.\nRecover the Eye and our services shall be yours - for whatever time remains for your side.\nReturn to me once you acquire the eye so that I may examine you.\n<Master Ryson grins.>\nStart Syndicate Master Ryson Alterac Valley End Syndicate Master Ryson Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6847","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7167":{"id":7167,"t":"The Eye of Command","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Insignia Rank 5","desc":"Drek'Thar sings your praises. Kalimdor is abuzz with tales of your heroics. The Warchief glows - your stalwart defense of our clan has pleased him greatly.\nYou have earned the Eye of Command.\nPresent your insignia, Commander ‹name›.\n<Warmaster Laggrond salutes>","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 6\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Drek'Thar sings your praises. Kalimdor is abuzz with tales of your heroics. The Warchief glows - your stalwart defense of our clan has pleased him greatly.\nYou have earned the Eye of Command.\nPresent your insignia, Commander ‹name›.","done":"Channel the power of the insignia. Let the enemy hear your words. The might of the Horde is unquestionable!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"847":{"id":847,"t":"Guile of the Raptor","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tor'gan.","desc":"This... this power.... Is this the power of the shamans that Tor'gan tried to show me? I must say, it is interesting. Tell Tor'gan that he has convinced me... for the time being. I will listen to what he has to say.","rew":"You will receive:\nCall of the Raptor\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"When the enchantment wears off, I will speak with Gor'mul. My thanks to you for your help in returning Gor'mul to the land of the living. I have no doubt he thanks you greatly as well.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":72.6,"y":33.9,"n":"Gor'mul","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"687":{"id":687,"t":"Theldurin the Lost","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Theldurin the Lost.","desc":"Theldurin the Lost was once a member of our order, the Twilight's Hammer. But he lost his mind and scorned our teachings. And before he fled from us, he stole the scroll of Myzrael! We could not catch him, but rumors say he hides in the Badlands, gibbering and mad.\nTo bring the Lady back to us, you must find the scroll. And to do that, you must find Theldurin.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","done":"Hello. Hello, hello hello hello hello HELLO!\nI'm sorry - wait, no I'm not! Don't be rude!\nOh no...that was crazy talk.\nBut...sometimes being crazy is my only solace.\nDun Morogh Arathi Highlands Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.5,"y":35.6,"n":"Zaruk","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1007":{"id":1007,"t":"The Ancient Statuette","lv":20,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Ancient Statuette to Talen, in his camp near the Zoram Strand.\nAncient Statuette Ancient Statuette","desc":"I would charge you with a task, ‹name›.\nI was on my small vessel, skimming over the submerged ruins of Zoram, when naga attacked me, surging from the water and tearing at me with their claws! I fled, carrying what supplies I could to make this meager camp.\nBut when I reached the shore and ran... my prized possession was lost.\nPlease, ‹name›, find the site of my ambush, along the coast to the north, and search for an ancient statuette. It is the reason I have braved the dangers of the Zoram Strand.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you found the statuette, ‹name›?","done":"You found it! Thank you, ‹name›!\nThe old city of Zoram holds many secrets, and this statuette may be the key to many of them.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":14.8,"y":31.3,"n":"Talen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"98287":{"id":98287,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.\nLevel 6 , requires level 4 Difficulty 4 9 12 Side Alliance Quest ID 98287","cats":["camping"]},"96047":{"id":96047,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.2,"y":52.6,"n":"Thamner Pol","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97967":{"id":97967,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Fenn Fairweather in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill as a fisherman.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45,"y":48.4,"n":"Fenn Fairweather","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96607":{"id":96607,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Eleanor's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94287":{"id":94287,"t":"Craftsmans writ fire goggles","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Fire Goggles\nFire Goggles","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Fire Goggles, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Fire Goggles Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94287","cats":["crafting"]},"1167":{"id":1167,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":28,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.","desc":"Before confronting Athrikus, it would probably be wise for you to consult with Balthule. I have no doubt he has been vigilant in his watch of the Tower, and he may have information about recent developments.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, it's good to see you again, ‹name›! The strangest things have been happening around here, I'm glad you showed up!\nIt was very strange, ‹name›. Everything seemed normal--well, as normal as things get around here--and then suddenly there was a blinding flash of light from the upper room of the tower. Then came the screams. The cries split the air, and lightning struck the ground from time to time. What's going on?\nAshenvale Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6127":{"id":6127,"t":"The Principal Source","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler to draw a sample of water from a pool at the top of the peak.\nDeliver the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads, Barrens.\nFilled Dreadmist Peak Sampler\nProvided: Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler","desc":"Dreadmist Peak to the northwest of the Crossroads is most likely a primary candidate as to the source of the spread of the poison. Its airy peaks have pools of water that influence the weather patterns. I suspect the water is now tainted by the demon-worshipping Burning Blade.\nUse this sampler to draw water from the pool at the very top of the peak. Once filled, deliver it to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads. He is the one that requested our aid, and you will work with him to address this malady.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You are the one that the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade sent, yes? This is most fortuitous for us! We are stymied in our effort to bring balance to the sickly gazelles that wander the northern Barrens; we're happy for all the help we can get.\nDo you have the sample of water that Dendrite Starblaze said you'd have? He notified me that you'd draw one so we could work on a cure together...","done":"By my ancestors, this water is disgusting! No wonder the gazelles are sick.\nSomething is polluting the water, and in turn beginning to wreck the northern Barrens ecosystem. Sick gazelles have been sighted all north of the east-west road here. While this water is most likely a primary source of the sickness spreading, there's something else at work here.\nThis water, believe it or not, will help us formulate a cure. While I research this water, I have need of some items to formulate a cure...\nMoonglade The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"287":{"id":287,"t":"Frostmane Hold","lv":9,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Explore Frostmane Hold, and kill 5 Frostmane Headhunters for Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.\nFrostmane Headhunter slain : 0/ 5","desc":"I'm behind on my report, and could use your help, ‹name›. I just managed to find where the trolls are holed up, but I saw so many trolls, I was afraid to go in.\nHere's what I need... Go down to the cave, poke around inside, kill a few of the trolls, then come back here.\nTake the road north out of Kharanos, when you get to the bridge, follow the frozen river west until you reach Iceflow Lake. You'll find Brewnall Village on the west bank. The Hold is southwest of the village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWarm Winter Robe Stone Buckler\nExperience: 600\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"You can't find it? My directions were very clear! We don't have much time, you've got to hurry! Don't come back until you've found the cave.","done":"Ah, ‹name›! I didn't think you'd have much trouble finding the place, my directions are excellent, you know...\nLet me just finish up my report then.\n<He brings out some paper and scribbles on it momentarily.>\nThere! Well, haha, now this certainly is funny... I don't suppose, ‹name›, that you would mind doing one last favor for me?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.7,"y":53.8,"n":"Senir Whitebeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"98447":{"id":98447,"t":"The valor family","lv":27,"min":18,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the cause of the Valor family ghosts in Raven Hill for Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.\nRaven Hill investigated","desc":"Despite you putting down the Valor family ghosts, the reports of attacks have not ceased. It was a good gamble, but perhaps we did not settle their unfinished business after all.\nFrom my research, it sounds like this family all went missing at the same time. Whatever trauma caused their spirits to be chained to this realm must have happened all at once.\nOur only clue is where you found the book. Return to Raven Hill and see what you can find. Maybe bringing their weapons will spark something.\nDuskwood Open the zone on the world map Level 27 , requires level 18 Difficulty 18 23 25 30 35 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 98447","cats":["duskwood"]},"5247":{"id":5247,"t":"Fragments of the Past","lv":57,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Enchanted Thorium Bar, 5 Crystal Restore, and a Vial of Dire Water to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.\nEnchanted Thorium Bar\n5 Crystal Restore\nVial of Dire Water\nProvided: Empty Water Vial","desc":"I will be able to help you, if recreating the artifact is truly what you wish to do.\nTo seal the pieces back together, I will need items with strong magical qualities. An enchanted thorium bar and five crystal restore... You'll also need to collect some water from what might seem an unlikely place... Find the dire pool along Eldreth Row at Dire Maul in Feralas, and fill this vial.\nWhile you are gone, I will attempt to glean from these pages the knowledge I need to repair the damage done to the relic.","rew":"Experience: 6,000\n+25 reputation with Alliance","back":"The relic must be placed in the hands of only the most trustworthy. It can not be stolen again...","done":"Using these elements, I can fuse the fragments together... to hopefully what they once were.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":46.5,"y":16,"n":"Aurora Skycaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"47":{"id":47,"t":"Gold Dust Exchange","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Gold Dust to Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire. Gold Dust is gathered from Kobolds in Elwynn Forest.\n10 Gold Dust Kobold Geomancer 50 % , Kobold Tunneler 50 % , Goldtooth 50 % , Kobold Miner 50 %","desc":"The Kobolds in these parts sometimes carry Gold Dust on them. I could really use the stuff - bring me a load of it and I'll give you the best price in town...best price in town!\nYou can find kobolds in the Fargodeep Mine to the south, and around the Jasperlode Mine to the northeast.","rew":"You will receive:\nBag of Marbles\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Psst! You have that Gold Dust for me...for me?","done":"Thanks for the dust, ‹name›. Here's your cash, and...here is a token from associates of mine. You might find it useful...useful.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":67.3,"n":"Remy \"Two Times\"","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3647":{"id":3647,"t":"Membership Card Renewal","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -2g instead of 0.","rew":"You will receive:\nGnome Engineer Membership Card","back":"In order to renew your membership card, you will need to pay the renewal fee of two gold pieces.","done":"Since you're a practitioner of Gnomish engineering and are in good standing, I am able to renew a lapsed membership card for the fee of two gold pieces. Once this fee is paid, you will be reissued a new membership card. This will allow access to Gnomish engineering schemata from appropriate trainers.\nThis card will last for two weeks of activity, at the end of which your membership fees will become due again! If you want to access schemata, you'll need to bring your dues out of arrears.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"8447":{"id":8447,"t":"Waking Legends","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Keeper Remulos at the Moonglade to cleanse the Nightmare Engulfed Object.","desc":"The waters of Lake Elune'ara should dissolve the nightmares engulfing this object. Give me a moment to perform the cleansing, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nMalfurion's Signet Ring\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Take his ring, ‹name›. It has served its purpose for Malfurion. It shall now serve a new purpose for you...","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["epic"]},"95647":{"id":95647,"t":"Lost in the thicket things","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Ardin Grassman in the Excavation Sites.\nLearn what happened to Ardin Grassman","desc":"My husband, Ardin, has a rare gift for sensing nature. He'll scale any peak to gather the herbs and flowers I need for my alchemy, keeping our shelves and pantry stocked.\nBut I fear he's wandered into trouble. An excavation crew passed through seeking supplies. They spoke, among other things, of towering grasses unlike anything they'd ever seen. Those were what he told me he had to go see for himself. He's been gone too long!\nIf you learn anything of him, I'd be grateful.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.8,"y":58.6,"n":"Caitlin Grassman","s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4447":{"id":4447,"t":"Corrupted Night Dragon","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a night dragon plant. The fruits that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 4 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Night Dragon. It immediately begins to shed it's corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.6,"y":30.4,"n":"Corrupted Night Dragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5887":{"id":5887,"t":"Salve via Hunting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Corrupted Soul Shard Ulathek 35 % , Xavaric 35 % , Prince Xavalis 35 % , Jaedenar Legionnaire 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.\nIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, ‹name›! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3567":{"id":3567,"t":"To the Top","lv":25,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"Would you like to see the view atop one of the twin colossals? I can send you there, ‹race›.\nDo consider how you will get down, though. This is a one way trip only.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":45.8,"y":16.5,"n":"Marli Wishrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"4127":{"id":4127,"t":"Boat Wreckage","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Feathermoon Stronghold and show Ginro Hearthkindle the Discarded Knife you have found.\nDiscarded Knife\nProvided: Discarded Knife","desc":"Running your hand along the mud, your fingers graze the handle of a knife. It looks well cared for, and it might be safe to assume that whoever was on the boat might have lost it. Perhaps the large chunk of the missing boat might have something to do with the loss.\nYou grab the knife, remembering that Ginro Hearthkindle in the Feathermoon Stronghold instructed you to return to him with any found clues. You get the feeling, however, that you are not quite alone in the water...","rew":"Experience: 380","back":"Ah, welcome back ‹name›. I hope that you were able to uncover some clue as to Raschal's ultimate fate, as tragic as that may be.","done":"Interesting... I believe that this is Raschal's knife. You say you found it at the bottom of the water, along with his boat? Well, just the knife's discovery might not be enough to connect this to Raschal's disappearance; we do, however, have an unconventional option available to us to try and learn more.\nHave you ever heard of psychometry?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":45.4,"y":65,"n":"Wrecked Row Boat","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2767":{"id":2767,"t":"Rescue OOX-22/FE!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort OOX-22/FE to the dock along the Forgotten Coast, then report to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.","desc":"The gnome's voice crackles once again from the robot:\n\"I need to move OOX-22/FE to an open, safe place so it can begin a lengthy take-off procedure. It has built-in cloaking, but I need time on my end to make it operational again. Escort the robot from its current location to, let's say, the dock along the Forgotten Coast! That should be a perfect place, and long enough, to get things online!\"\n\"Escort it safely to the dock, and then come talk to me in Booty Bay! Oglethorpe Obnoticus - out!\"","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFailed Flying Experiment Chainlink Towel\nExperience: 4,850\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Yes, I'm Oglethorpe Obnoticus, master inventor at your service! Now, is there something I could assist you with?","done":"Oh, YOU'RE the great savior of OOX-22/FE! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more development, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of extra rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in manufacture costs!\nPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Thank you again for your generous assistance ‹name›, my robots and I are in your debt!\nFeralas Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":53.4,"y":55.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-22/FE","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6607":{"id":6607,"t":"Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish:\nMisty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nA Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace.\nFeralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas.\nSavage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\nReturn to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!\nFeralas Ahi\nMisty Reed Mahi Mahi\nSar'theris Striker\nSavage Coast Blue Sailfin","desc":"Can't say I really enjoy fishin' much. Figure I been at it for a good 20 or 30 years now.\nI reckon people are driven to do what they do for different reasons.\nNow, I'm not saying you need to fish for 30 years or catch every fish in the sea to become a master fisherman. I reckon you just need to be determined - determined enough to sit on your duff for hours at a time, doin' nothin'.\nI'll tell you what, catch me a few rare fish and I'll teach you a thing or two. Here's a list:","rew":"You will learn: Fishing\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Anything bitin' today?","done":"Now that's a fine catch!\nCome over here, lemme show you how to set a few lines.\nDustwallow Marsh Feralas Swamp of Sorrows Desolace Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":58.6,"y":60.1,"n":"Nat Pagle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"2927":{"id":2927,"t":"The Day After","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos.","desc":"You don't think I was always bald, do you? No sir/ma'am! It was the radiation leak in Gnomeregan that caused this tragic hair loss. Before that day, I had the only gnomefro in all of Azeroth.\n<Gnoarn shakes his fist in the air.>\nDamn those damned dirty troggs - damn them all!!\nPerhaps it's not too late, ‹name›. We may still be able to save it - the city I mean! Speak to Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos. He and his partner Razzle are working on a solution.","rew":"Experience: 220\n+10 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"I thought the loss of that outstanding head of hair would have been the end of him for sure, but he survived!\nI was standing right next to him when he was hit by the radiation bolt. Those delightful brown locks of hair hit the floor in clumps! Clusters! The horror of it all was only compounded when Gnoarn completely freaked out! Oh yes, freaked out I say! Gnoarn touched his bald head in disbelief, the look in his eyes screamed revenge, ‹name›! Then he turned his anger towards the troggs!\n<Ozzie cringes.>","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Gnoarn","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.9,"y":49.4,"n":"Ozzie Togglevolt","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"527":{"id":527,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Hillsbrad Farmhands, 6 Hillsbrad Farmers, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nHillsbrad Farmer slain : 0/ 6\nHillsbrad Farmhand slain : 0/ 6\nFarmer Ray slain\nFarmer Getz slain","desc":"Stand at attention while addressing me, ‹class›.\nI am under direct command of Varimathras. We are to quell the human infestation until our apothecaries can develop the new plague.\nOur information leads us to believe that the town of Hillsbrad is vulnerable to attack. Your first assignment is aimed at disrupting their food supply and infrastructure.\nTravel west. Raid the northernmost farms of Hillsbrad Fields. Make sure that the landowners, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz, are executed as well.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"As High Executor of Tarren Mill, under the direct command of Varimathras and the Dark Lady, you are subject to follow my command.\nPerhaps you take this war with the Alliance lightly? If such is the case I should behead you right here and now. Otherwise, travel west to the town of Hillsbrad and wage battle against the humans, as ordered.\nDismissed.","done":"At ease, ‹class›. I see you have returned from battle. My sources tell me you performed well on the Hillsbrad front.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"3087":{"id":3087,"t":"Etched Parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Etched Parchment and speak to Jen'shan in the Valley of Trials.\nEtched Parchment\nProvided: Etched Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the hunter trainer Jen'shan. She would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Ah, so you come at last. Good. Jen'shan be waitin' for you.\nMany tink it be an easy path, but Jen'shan tell you dat not true. Mastering da beasts of Durotar and beyond take as much skill as masterin' the arcane arts or speakin' to our ancestors.\nFirin' a bow or rifle may not be as dangerous to you as castin' a spell, but it sure be as dangerous to your enemy.","done":"When we finish speakin', you should talk to da rest of da citizens in da Valley. They ask you to do tings for them... tings that will test your skill and teach you some of da dangers of this land.\nAs you grow in experience and wisdom, you be needin' Jen'shan to show you better techniques and skills. Come back to Jen'shan often. I will let you know what I can teach you.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Jen'shan","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9247":{"id":9247,"t":"The Keeper's Call","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 60.","obj":"Take the Letter from the Keeper of the Rolls to him at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Letter from the Keeper of the Rolls\nProvided: A Letter from the Keeper of the Rolls","desc":"‹name›,\nIn times past you have served the interests of the Argent Dawn, always to the best of your abilities. Now, once again, we sound the clarion call in our time of greatest need.\n‹name›, please report to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands if you are willing to aid us once more.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Wizard Oil Consecrated Sharpening Stone\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Ah, ‹name›, it is good to see you.","done":"Simply by answering the call, we are in your debt, ‹name›. The Argent Dawn is certain that through your shining example, others that are here to aid us will gain great insight into how best to throw back this Scourge Invasion!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"7807":{"id":7807,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Gnomeregan Exiles for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":28.8,"n":"Bubulo Acerbus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2847":{"id":2847,"t":"Wild Leather Armor","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Leather to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"‹name›, you're becoming quite skilled as a leatherworker! I know some patterns you might be interested in... Wild Leather armor! Wild Leather taps into the potent and chaotic properties of wildvines, found in areas of lush vegetation and on some of the creatures there. The armor made using it is second to none for people of your skill, guaranteed.\nI'll teach this to you, but you'll be working for me for a while. The first cost is simply ten pieces of thick leather. After this, we'll talk specifics.","rew":"Experience: 1,950","back":"Like I said, you'll be working for me while you learn about Wild Leather armor. Because wildvines are both potent and chaotic, it yields a random but strong benefit to the already strong armor you will be making. This knowledge, however, was not easy for me to come by.\nThe initial cost to begin this process is ten pieces of thick leather.\nOnce that is done, we'll get to the work you need to do in order to obtain the patterns.","done":"Well ‹name›, I'm glad to have you on board. You've made a smart decision as a leatherworker; those who wear leather armor will be clamoring to you once you learn how to make any of the Wild Leather armor pieces.\nLet's get to work - where do you want to start?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"7487":{"id":7487,"t":"Attunement to the core","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Venture to the Molten Core entry portal in Blackrock Depths and recover a Core Fragment. Return to Lothos Riftwaker in Blackrock Mountain when you have recovered the Core Fragment.\nCore Fragment","desc":"Rifts stir, tear, and collapse all around us, ‹race›. Not two paces from where I stand is a tear leading through the depths of Blackrock Mountain, into the maw of the Firelord.\nSurprised? Pity... The mortal races cannot comprehend that which they cannot see, touch, or feel.\nI assure you, the portal is there and access is possible.\nI've piqued your interest? Attunement is simple. Venture into Blackrock Depths and retrieve a core fragment. Return it to me and I shall attune your essence with the portal.\nLevel 60 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 56 58 Side Both factions Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 7487","cats":["molten-core-dungeon"]},"767":{"id":767,"t":"Rite of Vision","lv":6,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zarlman Two-Moons in Bloodhoof Village.","desc":"The Rite of Vision, one of the Rites of the Earthmother, will help guide you toward earning the respect of the elders of Thunder Bluff.\nOur people have learned that the land is our most holy provider. In order to take part in the ritualistic vision, you must speak with the spiritual leader of the village, Zarlman Two-Moons.","rew":"Experience: 55\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"I sensed you would be coming to me, ‹class›. I can always recognize one who is trying to pass the Rites of the Earthmother.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":63.4,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":61.2,"n":"Zarlman Two-Moons","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9087":{"id":9087,"t":"Dreamwalker Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreamwalker Legguards if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Legguards, 20 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 8 Cured Rugged Hides and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Legguards\n20 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n8 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Legguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"As promised, Dreamwalker Legguards.\n<Rayne hands you the armor.>","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5727":{"id":5727,"t":"Hidden Enemies","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Lieutenant's Insignia to Neeru Fireblade and speak to him. Gauge if he believes you are a member of the Burning Blade and then return to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nProvided: Lieutenant's Insignia","desc":"Now let us see if this insignia you found is worth the effort.\nThere is a warlock within the city who believes he has my trust. He does not know that I realize where his true loyalties lie. He is in fact the leader of the Burning Blade. But do not rush off to do battle with him; he has a purpose, and we shall use him against our enemies.\nTake this insignia to him in the Cleft of Shadow here in Orgrimmar, speak to him and see if he believes you are one of his own, then return to me here.","rew":"Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Well, ‹class›? Does he believe our ploy, or are things worse than I had first estimated?\nProving valuable to Neeru will make our infiltration of the Shadow Council much easier. He will have plenty of information that we can use to route out those who would destroy all we have built in Durotar.","done":"Excellent! Most excellent, ‹class›!\nWhat you have done this day is only the first step in a much broader foundation--a foundation that we will build the destruction of the Shadow Council on, once and for all.\nTell me all he said... and leave not one word out--it may be more important than you realize.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8367":{"id":8367,"t":"For Great Honor","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor, 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor and 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor","desc":"Serving the Horde in one of the great battles against the Alliance is a source of great honor! The few however, that have served the Horde in ALL of our active battlefronts are our truly great fighters. We shall vanquish our opponents, not by fighting isolated skirmishes, but by waging a well-coordinated war.\nGo forth and crush the Alliance in Arathi Basin, Alterac Valley, Eye of the Storm and Warsong Gulch! For Honor! For the Horde!","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+200 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+150 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+150 reputation with The Defilers","back":"Arathi is still wet with the blood of great warriors and the clash of steel still rings throughout Alterac. Do not waste my time unless you bring news from the front!","done":"Your trials have not been easy, but your courage did not escape you and your strength did not fail. Part with past tokens of victory, ‹class›. None shall need them as a reminder of your worth. Stand up straight, ‹name›. Today you will walk with great pride for you are a hero!\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8927":{"id":8927,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Wildheart Belt and a set of Wildheart Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nWildheart Belt Scholomance Handler 5.2 % in Scholomance , The Ravenian 4 % in Scholomance , Spectral Teacher 3.8 % in Scholomance , Spectral Researcher 1.5 % in Scholomance and 4 more\nWildheart Gloves Smolderthorn Berserker 4.5 % , Rage Talon Dragonspawn 3.8 % , Firebrand Pyromancer 2.4 % , Scarshield Raider 2.1 % and 4 more","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Belt Feralheart Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9007":{"id":9007,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Wildheart Cowl and Wildheart Vest.\nWildheart Cowl Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nWildheart Vest General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Cowl Feralheart Vest\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Wildheart pieces in exchange for your new Feralheart Cowl and Vest?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1647":{"id":1647,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the outer ring of Ironforge for John Turner.","desc":"Your task then, ‹name›, is to find someone here in Ironforge that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.\nDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light. I will remain here in the temple for your return. Other paladins will need my guidance also.","rew":"Experience: 460","done":"THE ORPHANAGE OF STOR... oh, sorry, didn't mean to shout at you, sir.\nMy name is John Turner. How are you?\nGood, good, glad to hear things go well for you. I've had a long day of work already, and I miss my wife terribly, but that's the price you have to pay when there are mouths to feed and backs to clothe.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":31,"n":"John Turner","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7647":{"id":7647,"t":"Judgment and Redemption","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance. Doing so will bring forth the spirits you must judge. Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver. Defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the fallen charger.\nGive the Charger's Redeemed Soul and the Blessed Enchanted Barding to Darkreaver's Fallen Charger.\nCharger's Redeemed Soul\nBlessed Arcanite Barding Risen Construct in Scholomance , Petrified Treant\nProvided: Lord Grayson's Satchel","desc":"Take this satchel - in it are the items you will need for your task.\nUse the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to bring forth accursed spirits that must be judged. Use your judgments wisely during this trial - they will prove more potent than you realize. After the spirits, the death knight will appear; defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the charger. Only then ‹name›, will you be able to redeem it and place your barding upon your new steed!\nGood luck!","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The spirit of the fallen charger looks upon you with a mournful gaze. Sad, almost hollow eyes look at you as though all hope was lost to it.","done":"A glimmer of life - long vacant from the poor beast - shines in its eyes as you hand its judged soul back to it. You feel a holy rush of power surge around you as you place the barding on its back, having judged the charger redeemed. The charger nuzzles your hand as the burdens of the past are lifted from the beast. You now feel as though you could call upon this beast to serve as your steed, should the need arise.\nYou have claimed your epic charger, ‹class›! Congratulations!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5647":{"id":5647,"t":"A Lack of Fear","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from A Lack of Fear.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"Your race is so very strong, ‹name›. We are proud to call you allies. And as each day's sun sets, you and your kin grow closer to not only finding your true origins, but find great confidence that you are on the right path in so many things. That feeling must make you feel so triumphant.\nWord came from Ironforge just recently. It asked that you return there and speak to High Priest Rohan in the Mystic Ward. I would not keep him waiting. May Elune guide your travels.","rew":"You will learn: Fear Ward\nExperience: 390","done":"You've got the makings of a great ‹class›, ‹name›. Keep up the good work!\nYou've already shown you're ready for battle. Perhaps it's time we taught ya a little somethin' more.\nDarnassus Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.3,"y":88.7,"n":"Lariia","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"127":{"id":127,"t":"Selling Fish","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Spotted Sunfish to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.\n10 Spotted Sunfish Squiddic 45 % , Murloc Shorestriker 45 % , Murloc Scout 45 % , Murloc Minor Tidecaller 45 % and 3 more","desc":"Lake Everstill is famous for its spotted sunfish. There's always demand for them...and I'm running low!\nBring me a batch of 10 and I'll barter well for them. If you can't fish yourself, then...maybe you can get them off the murlocs!","rew":"You will receive:\nMurloc Fin Soup Recipe: Murloc Fin Soup 5 Fishliver Oil\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have some sunfish for me, eh?","done":"Pleasure doin' business with you, matey!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":22.6,"y":47.4,"n":"Dockmaster Baren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"2607":{"id":2607,"t":"The Touch of Zanzil","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Doc Mixilpixil in the cellar of the Barracks.","desc":"It appears as if you've brought back more information than even I expected. This certainly is a strange turn of events, ‹name›.\nA cure? Hrm... Go down to the cellar and speak with Doc Mixilpixil - he may be able to help.","done":"It's about time! Just put the cheese on the table and skedaddle. Osborne will pay you on the way out.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Doc Mixilpixil","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"7727":{"id":7727,"t":"Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It","lv":49,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Incendosaurs.\nYou will find Incendosaurs occupying the lava pools inside the Slag Pit. The Slag Pit can be found in the Cauldron of the Searing Gorge.\nReturn to Hansel Heavyhands in the Searing Gorge when you have killed enough Incendosaurs.\nIncendosaur slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Bunions, lad/lass. Me bunions got bunions. How am I supposed to do any sort of killin' with me feet in such disarray? That's why ye're gonna help.\nScrange and Burninate tasked me to kill these things so they can send some expeditionary teams down into the Slag Pit lava pools to do some explorin'. Supposedly some incendosaurs or some such nonsense down there causin' all kinds o' problems. Now move along an' don't come back 'til the incendosaur population be extinct.","rew":"You will receive:\nLuffa\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"<Hansel is busily rubbing his bunions.>\nDon't just stand there, grab some oil and a luffa and get to scrubbin' these bunions.\nYe don't have a luffa? Well then! Perhaps it's time I sent you out to find a luffa?%\nHey, where are ye goin'?","done":"Oh me achin' feets.\nI figured since ye didn't have a luffa...","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.6,"y":27.8,"n":"Hansel Heavyhands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8767":{"id":8767,"t":"A Gently Shaken Gift","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nGently Shaken Gift","done":"This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:\nTo a very special ‹race› ‹class›.\nDun Morogh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Gently Shaken Gift","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.3,"y":69.4,"n":"Gently Shaken Gift","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"92847":{"id":92847,"t":"Corrupting tears","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3 Petrified Bark\n3 Imbued Tears\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"Outsider, did you notice the weapon that the outcast necromancers held in their hands? We will ensure the Gelkis will not live long enough to master the ways of necromancy, but their methods of channeling caught my interest. They even use those same crystals Warug asked you to steal.\nI think we can use this technique to our advantage. Venture back into the valley to recover some wood from the accursed trees, and see if Warug will part with some of his crystals. I will make staves from them.\nLevel 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92847\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay","cats":["shendralas"]},"8287":{"id":8287,"t":"A Terrible Purpose","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Decoded Tablet Parchment to Commander Mar'alith.\nDecoded Tablet Transcription\nProvided: Decoded Tablet Transcription","desc":"Ok, here we are... a pretty valuable chunk of information, I must say! I've seen the Cenarion Circle forces arrive at Silithus. They plan to drive the Twilight's Hammer out, don't they? This will help.\nTake this parchment to their leader, Commander Mar'alith. Soon the Twilight's Hammer will be vanquished and I will be outside their grasp for good!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"What is this you bring to me, ‹name›?","done":"This is very interesting information indeed, ‹name›. This sheds some light on the presence of the Twilight's Hammer in Silithus and will undoubtedly help us in our struggle against them. Your efforts will be handsomely rewarded, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":67.2,"y":69.8,"n":"Hermit Ortell","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8687":{"id":8687,"t":"Target: Hive'Zora Tunnelers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Zora Tunnelers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing VII in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing VII\nHive'Zora Tunneler slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing VII","desc":"Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora. You have been selected to target Hive'Zora tunnelers. Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"447":{"id":447,"t":"A Recipe For Death","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Grizzled Bear Hearts and 6 samples of Skittering Blood and deliver them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\n6 Grizzled Bear Heart Giant Grizzled Bear 80 % , Old Vicejaw 80 % , Ferocious Grizzled Bear 80 %\n6 Skittering Blood Moss Stalker 80 % , Mist Creeper 80 % , Krethis Shadowspinner 80 %","desc":"Arthas's numbers are overwhelming. But with a New Plague we could eradicate both the Scourge Army and the Human infestation once and for all.\nMy studies have proven that spider blood combined with a toxin derived from a grizzled bear heart results in a deadly elixir. Collect samples from the spiders in the Skittering Dark to the northwest and from the bears wandering throughout Silverpine Forest. Deliver the reagents to Master Apothecary Faranell of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity.","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Senggin Root\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Hail, ‹class›. What business do you have with the Royal Apothecary Society?","done":"How good of Apothecary Renferrel to send you to me, ‹name›. These samples will indeed prove useful to the cause. I will begin studying their toxic and contaminable properties at once.\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"78127":{"id":78127,"t":"The dalaran digest","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"The Dalaran Digest, Vol. 23","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nThe Dalaran Digest, Vol. 23 (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1087":{"id":1087,"t":"Cenarius' Legacy","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 4 Sons of Cenarius, 4 Daughters of Cenarius and 4 Cenarion Botanists for Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.\nSon of Cenarius slain : 0/ 4\nDaughter of Cenarius slain : 0/ 4\nCenarion Botanist slain : 0/ 4","desc":"You cannot imagine the hatred I possess for this wretched land. The ilk of Cenarius and the kaldorei druids at the peak employ their pathetic powers to stifle the flow of magic, even so far south of their pathetic holdings... their beloved forests.\nWould that I could return to Jaedenar and exult in the flow of magic, but my master will not allow me to return until my work is done.\nI have no doubt you love the night elves and their allies as little as I. Aid me, and both our ends might be satisfied.","rew":"Experience: 1,500","back":"Here, channeling magic is like drawing water from a well with a bucket full of holes.","done":"Already I can feel it... yes... power so sweet... the rushing flood. The kaldorei are foolish to spurn the gifts of this world, to reject the coursing of magic as it flows singing through your veins.\nWhat a pale mockery life is without its burning embrace!","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":45.9,"y":60.4,"n":"Braelyn Firehand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1247":{"id":1247,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Elling Trias in Stormwind.","desc":"So yeah... um... I might know something 'bout that meeting at Addle's Stead. Happened a few weeks back I think. I really didn't have any part in it. Me part was done when plan A failed... damn adventurers.\nThe guy we got on the inside for plan B came out of Menethil; guy called Slim. That's all I know regarding their backup plan.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"Good to see you're still alive, ‹name›. So, it went well with Dashel then, huh?\nI've been reading up more on this plan of theirs, and although it doesn't state the name of the diplomat they were after, it does talk about this plan B they enacted after failing on their first attempt to capture him.\nThis Slim that Dashel mentioned doesn't have any other name written here, but if you say he's in Menethil, then that's a start.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":74.3,"y":59.2,"n":"Dashel Stonefist","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"207":{"id":207,"t":"Kurzen's Mystery","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the 4 tablets and bring their legends back to Brother Nimetz.\nThe First Troll Legend Moon Over the Vale\nThe Second Troll Legend Gri'lek the Wanderer , Gri'lek the Wanderer\nThe Third Troll Legend Fall of Gurubashi\nThe Fourth Troll Legend The Emperor's Tomb","desc":"Colonel Kurzen was once a great, noble man - I must find what caused his fall into depravity! He may be under the sway of troll magic. To confirm this, I must study some of their legends.\nThere are 4 tablets hidden within the troll ruins of Stranglethorn. I must see what is written on these tablets! Transcribe their markings and bring the transcriptions back to me.\nThe first tablet is in the Bal'lal Ruins, the second is in the Vile Reef, and the third and fourth are in the Ruins of Zul'Kunda.","rew":"Experience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›! Do you have the troll legends? I must know their secrets!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I will study these legends to see if there is some link between the trolls and the evil that has possessed Colonel Kurzen.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.8,"y":3.6,"n":"Brother Nimetz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"607":{"id":607,"t":"Return to MacKinley","lv":41,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Shaky's Payment to \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley.\nShaky's Payment\nProvided: Shaky's Payment","desc":"Here, take this pouch and give it to Sea Wolf. And tell him I meant to pay him back! I swear!!\nI just got a little drunk and lost my way, and...you know how things are. He'll understand - you don't have to get rough!","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Here here, ‹name›. Did you get Shaky's payment?","done":"Heh heh, well done! And when you showed Shaky those giblets, how hard did he shake?\nHah! He's so easy to read, when I play cards with him I can't help but win!\nThanks for your help, ‹name›. Now it's your turn to get paid...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":73.6,"n":"\"Shaky\" Phillipe","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"927":{"id":927,"t":"The Moss-twined Heart","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Moss-twined Heart to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.\nMoss-twined Heart\nProvided: Moss-twined Heart","desc":"The heart of Blackmoss the Fetid is covered with a dark, oily moss. In fact, the only way to tell this is a heart is from its slow, rhythmic beat... A beat that continues even now.\nPerhaps Denalan will want to see this heart.","rew":"Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›! You have something for me?","done":"...What is this? A timberling heart?? It's covered with a foul moss!\nThank you for bringing this to me, ‹name›. I will examine the heart and, if fortune shines, determine the nature of the moss about it.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"79007":{"id":79007,"t":"And that note you found","lv":22,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide.","desc":"<The faint radiance of the embers darkening, you stumble across the remnants of a recent fire.\nAmidst the scattered provisions, you discover a blistered note.>\n\"Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.\"","rew":"You will receive:\nSwiftness Potion Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir\nExperience: 1,750","done":"As you stumble upon the remnants of yet another charred corpse, your gaze falls upon a message secured to a wooden plank.\nThe Barrens Westfall","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.4,"y":73.9,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":37.5,"y":50.7,"n":"Burned-Out Remains","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":37.5,"y":50.8,"n":"Nailed Plank","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4767":{"id":4767,"t":"Wind Rider","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Highperch Wyvern Eggs to Elu in Freewind Post.\n10 Highperch Wyvern Egg Highperch Wyvern Egg","desc":"I've been tasked to recruit more wyverns for the master wind riders. Their numbers are growing and I myself hope to become a wind rider one day. However, we cannot train enough wyverns to keep up with the demand. Perhaps you can help me, ‹name›.\nI need you to travel to Highperch to gather some wyvern eggs. From here, head northwest along the canyon walls to a ramp that will lead you into Highperch. Be careful, wyverns are very protective over their eggs and they will not be kind to intruders.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Heavy Armor Kit\nMoney: 19 0 gold, 19 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, have you retrieved the wyvern eggs that I seek? I'm really anxious to start my wind rider training!","done":"Perfect! With these eggs I hope to take the next step to become a wind rider. Here is a token of my appreciation; may good hunting always shine upon you, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":44.9,"y":48.9,"n":"Elu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"367":{"id":367,"t":"A New Plague","lv":6,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Apothecary Johaan in the town of Brill wants you to collect 5 Vials of Darkhound Blood.\n5 Darkhound Blood Decrepit Darkhound 35 % , Cursed Darkhound 35 % , Ravenous Darkhound 35 %","desc":"Lady Sylvanas has called upon the Royal Apothecary Society. The Dark Lady believes our knowledge coupled with the newfound magic will provide the key to Arthas's demise. She has challenged us to concoct a new plague, a plague deadlier than any ailment on Azeroth. This new disease will bring Arthas's Scourge Army to ruin.\nMy studies show that the blood of beasts might prove to be the key. Bring to me 5 vials of darkhound blood so I can test my theory.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Minor Troll's Blood Elixir\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you collected 5 vials of darkhound blood yet, ‹name›? Time is fleeting!","done":"You have done well, ‹name› and I thank you for your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4287":{"id":4287,"t":"The Eastern Pylon","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Discover the location of the Eastern Crystal Pylon in Un'Goro Crater.","desc":"During my stay here, I have heard strange rumors about mysterious pylons existing out in the wilderness of the crater, ‹name›. I guess that they are quite large, with crystals lining their interiors.\nAlthough I've never seen one, I can't help but think that the rumors are true -- and that the pylons have something to do with all the crystals we found\nSo why don't you help me put my curiosity to rest? Supposedly, there is one in the eastern area of the crater. Do you think you can find it?","rew":"Experience: 3,950","back":"Have you visited the pylon, ‹name›?","done":"Un'Goro is such a strange place, ‹name›. When you enter the crater, it's as if you are in a completely different world...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1487":{"id":1487,"t":"Deviate Eradication","lv":21,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,000 experience instead of 2,050, 1.95 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Ebru in the Wailing Caverns wants you to kill 7 Deviate Ravagers, 7 Deviate Vipers, 7 Deviate Shamblers and 7 Deviate Dreadfangs.\nDeviate Ravager slain : 0/ 7\nDeviate Viper slain : 0/ 7\nDeviate Shambler slain : 0/ 7\nDeviate Dreadfang slain : 0/ 7","desc":"Naralex had a noble goal.\nOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was. But something went terribly wrong.\nNaralex's dream turned into a nightmare and corrupt creatures began to inhabit the caverns.\nWhile some Disciples of Naralex seek to awake our master, my concern is with ridding these caves of the evil beasts.\nBrave the caverns, ‹name›, and eradicate the deviate spawn.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPattern: Deviate Scale Belt Sizzle Stick Dagmire Gauntlets\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,000","back":"‹name›, we, the Disciples of Naralex, need your help. Our numbers are dwindling with our master trapped in his twisted nightmare. We have not the forces necessary to deal with the corrupt creatures which now haunt these caverns.\nI beg of you, enter the caves and wage war on the deviate creatures!","done":"As a Disciple of Naralex, I commend your bravery, ‹name›.\nYour aid in ridding the caverns is the first step in our long plight to see the Barrens restored.\nThank you and may you prosper.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46,"y":35.7,"n":"Ebru","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"5407":{"id":5407,"t":"Invader's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Invader's Scourgestone Lorekeeper Polkelt in Scholomance , Rattlegore in Scholomance , Blood Steward of Kirtonos in Scholomance , Terrordale Spirit 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nEach valor token handed out to worthy recipients is a sign of the tide turning against the Scourge. With more and more heroes fighting the Scourge in their own lands, the Argent Dawn will assuredly be at the forefront when the time comes to wage war on the ultimate evil of the Scourge. I hope that the valor you've shown what it took to acquiring your token will carry the day then as well!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Argent Officer Garush","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5167":{"id":5167,"t":"Legplates of the Chromatic Defier","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To forge the Legplates of the Chromatic Defier, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor':\n1 Chromatic Carapace.\n10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales.\n10 Blood of Heroes.\n5 Skin of Shadow.\nItem #12871\n10 Brilliant Chromatic Scale\n10 Blood of Heroes\n5 Skin of Shadow","desc":"The carapace of a mature chromatic drake is needed to form the foundation of the leggings. Brilliant chromatic scales are then layered upon the wire frame and enchanted in the blood of heroes. Finally, the supple skin of shadow must be applied to the inner greaves.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLegguards of the Chromatic Defier Legplates of the Chromatic Defier\nExperience: 9,950","back":"Such an item has never been crafted!","done":"They will smell their kin as you enter their halls, ‹name›. Crush them with their own fear!\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.3,"y":66.6,"n":"Catalogue of the Wayward","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Jeziba","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5087":{"id":5087,"t":"Winterfall Runners","lv":57,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Winterfall Runners and stop them from delivering their shipment to Winterfall Village.\nWinterfall Crate Winterfall Runner","desc":"Very interesting, ‹name›...\nWhen this toxic substance is mixed with the water from the hot springs, it loses its toxicity, only retaining the ability to temporarily affect those that ingest it. This must be why the Winterfall protect the hot springs so fervently -- they need them to purify their firewater.\nWe need to stop this -- cut off contact between the Winterfall and the Deadwood. A group of runners walks the distance between their village and Felwood. Find and defeat them, and steal their shipment.","rew":"Experience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"We'll see what happens when the Winterfall don't get their firewater!","done":"<Donova examines the contents of the crate>\nI wonder if consuming this substance makes the furbolg more aggressive. They do seem much larger...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"8047":{"id":8047,"t":"The Heathen's Brand","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Heathen's Brand","rew":"You will receive:\nHeathen's Brand\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I must confess, I did not think you had the resolution to see this cause through, ‹class›. Zandalar now considers you an invaluable ally. Well done, indeed.\nGive me your brand and I shall once more amplify its power.","done":"Our beliefs differ but our cause is righteous. Strike down our foes, noble ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});